{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And you.</b> Because Moses was the priest of priests at the beginning, therefore the sense of 'bring near to you.' I have already hinted to you why Aaron was chosen to be consecrated to the Name — for the honor of the family of Nahshon, so that the priests would make atonement for the children of Israel. And there is nothing to say about Moses our master, for he was fleeing, and who would give him leisure [עברית], and moreover the burden of all Israel is upon Moses to teach them the commandments and to judge every difficult matter." "The vav of <b>to serve Me.</b> Extra, like the vav of חיתו שדי (Psalms 104:11), בנו בעור (Numbers 24:3). And the meaning of 'the sons of Aaron' — perhaps he had other sons besides these. And there is no doubt that the family of Aaron multiplied greatly, as stated in Numbers; therefore Israel gave them many cities, as written in the book of Joshua."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "Reading עברית literally as 'Hebrew'; the word is obscure in context and possibly corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:47.427146573Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}